288: \]
289: This computes the actual return on every fan (CF.18), including
290: \(j=0\). Its sequence has period seven: modulo 28 it equals
291: \(23+4j(j+1)\), and shifting \(j\) by seven changes this
292: by \(56j+224\). The seven consecutive values are
293: \[
294:                          23,3,19,15,19,3,23 .
295: \]
296: They give the exact range \(\{3,15,19,23\}\); the sequence
297: is not constant, so seven is its least positive period.
298: In particular
299: \(R_1=(\begin{smallmatrix}2&-1\\-1&1\end{smallmatrix})\)
300: has the actual positive return class three.
301: 
302: All original physical source and cap maps are carried through
303: the specified finite sequence for each \(j\). This proof assigns
304: no value to a fan outside its computed domain. The exact algebra
305: and repeated-basis/fan consistency checks are retained under
306: \path{code/part3_root/source_cusp_mutation_diagnostic.*}; their
307: first unsimplified symbolic-matrix equality attempt is preserved.
308: The written Cox/period maps, native-frame comparison and induction
309: are the proof for all \(j\). The active finite search starts only
310: from the proved \(P_0=1\) seed: at depth seven it checks
311: 210 basis states and 128 fan states, with no conflicting state
312: or failed integrality check. Four transitions to a target with
313: a separately retained fixed curve are left unevaluated.
314: The earlier exploratory two-seed output is retained separately;
315: its second fixed-star seed supplies no input to this proof.
